{"evt":"snapshot_stored","id":"codex/fix-costflow-durable-claim-session-provenance","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","subject":"Fix costflow durable claim session provenance","description":"Fix the remaining live /costflow attribution issue. Historical Codex tasks in buildGraph have t.session === 'codex', but their durable per-task .graph/claims/<task>.json files contain the real Codex session UUID in session_id. /costflow currently builds claims from g.tasks and passes t.session into taskTranscript, so it never sees the UUID and cannot resolve rollout-<timestamp>-<uuid>.jsonl. Update /costflow claim construction to prefer active overlay claimSessions[task], then durable git claim session_id from lib/git-claims.readLocalClaim(T.ws, task), then t.session. Use that attribution session for taskTranscript and claim.session, but do not change graph display/session semantics. Add a regression showing a task with t.session='codex', no overlay claimSession, and a local git claim session_id UUID resolves/splits the Codex rollout and subtracts catchall. Keep the fix surgical.","status":"pending","blockedBy":[],"owner":null,"metadata":{"synthetic_overlay_task":true,"created_by":"subconscious_assignment"},"snapshotted_at":"2026-06-23T04:32:57.599Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T04:32:58.512Z"}
